[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3393613564","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111521#issuecomment-3393613564","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111521","id":3393613564,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KRm78","user":{"login":"ARez2","id":75789249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1Nzg5MjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75789249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2","html_url":"https://github.com/ARez2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-11T19:33:38Z","updated_at":"2025-10-11T19:33:38Z","body":"Oh and I just noticed in the MRP, that the origin lines are broken too, but that is a separate issue.\n<img width=\"881\" height=\"692\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6cee7465-0838-4e1b-b6e0-00b54e903bf8\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3393613564/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3395220499","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111521#issuecomment-3395220499","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111521","id":3395220499,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KXvQT","user":{"login":"CodeSmith32","id":21373557,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzczNTU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21373557?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32","html_url":"https://github.com/CodeSmith32","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-12T18:50:45Z","updated_at":"2025-10-12T18:50:45Z","body":"Gotta say, that game looks sick!\n\nUnfortunately, yeah. You're experiencing [this same issue](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98655). Godot is built using floats by default. If you download the Godot source code, there is a DEFINE switch that switches it to use double instead. Sadly, I don't know of any mirrors to download prebuilt copies.\n\nWith that said, there are a few other steps you might need to take to get it working since shaders don't guarantee support for 64-bit precision. [This article](https://godotengine.org/article/emulating-double-precision-gpu-render-large-worlds/) goes through a practical solution using the double-build.\n\nAnother option might be to try what Flarkk suggested in issue https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98655#issuecomment-3038784064 &ndash; it could involve a bit of re-work, though, depending on your setup. :-/","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3395220499/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3405800107","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111521#issuecomment-3405800107","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111521","id":3405800107,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LAGKr","user":{"login":"ARez2","id":75789249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1Nzg5MjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75789249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2","html_url":"https://github.com/ARez2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T10:42:21Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T10:45:12Z","body":"Thanks! Yeah I already have found a solution for my case using sphere meshes instead of quads and then having a custom shader which uses the sphere normals to display a flipbook. That works really well without precision issues AFAIK. But for completeness sake, I wanted to create this issue as well.\n\nI am trying to avoid using origin shifting as in my case I want combat to happen over long distances so the player as well as the enemy should be loaded in at the same time and be able to fire bullets/ torpedoes at each other. I think that would be really annoying to do using origin shifting.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3405800107/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3406960017","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111521#issuecomment-3406960017","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111521","id":3406960017,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LEhWR","user":{"login":"NuclearPhoenixx","id":17517687,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTE3Njg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17517687?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx","html_url":"https://github.com/NuclearPhoenixx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T15:14:03Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T15:14:03Z","body":"Can confirm I have the same issue. Glad I found this relatively recent issue, otherwise 